Smoke test for `markdown-hr`. Lines marked HR-EXPECTED should render as `<hr>`. Lines marked NOT-HR should pass through as plain text (and the source character should appear literally).

## Should render as `<hr>`

HR-EXPECTED (3 dashes):

---

HR-EXPECTED (3 asterisks):

***

HR-EXPECTED (3 underscores):

___

HR-EXPECTED (more than 3):

------

HR-EXPECTED (3-space indent):

   ---

HR-EXPECTED (3 consecutive + extras with spaces):

--- - -

## Should NOT render as `<hr>` (falls through)

NOT-HR (only 2 dashes — falls through as plain text, then the next blank line ends the paragraph):

--

NOT-HR (trailing non-marker char):

---x

NOT-HR (mixed marker chars):

- * -

NOT-HR (4-space indent — CommonMark indented-code position):

    ---

NOT-HR (whitespace BEFORE the first 3 — not supported by literal-3-char open design):

- - -

NOT-HR (5 stars with spaces from the start):

* * * * *

NOT-HR (mid-paragraph dashes):

text --- more text on the same line
